# **1  Introduction**

## **1.1 Purpose**

This Software Requirements Specification (SRS) defines the functional, non-functional, data, interface, and deployment requirements for the Medical Imaging Diagnostic Pipeline — an end-to-end system that performs automated brain tumor segmentation from multi-modal MRI scans using the BraTS (Brain Tumor Segmentation) dataset. The document is intended to serve as the single authoritative reference for design, implementation, testing, and deployment decisions throughout the project lifecycle.

The system covers the full path from raw NIfTI MRI volumes to a deployed, containerized inference service with a web-based visualization front end, and is built to demonstrate production-grade engineering practices rather than a notebook-only prototype.

## **1.2 Scope**

The system, referred to throughout this document as the Pipeline, shall:

- Ingest and validate multi-modal MRI volumes (T1, T1ce, T2, FLAIR) in NIfTI format.

- Preprocess volumes through resampling, skull-stripping validation, intensity normalization, and patch extraction.

- Train and evaluate a 3D deep learning segmentation model (3D U-Net baseline, with an nnU-Net / Swin-UNETR extension path) to delineate tumor sub-regions: enhancing tumor (ET), tumor core (TC), and whole tumor (WT).

- Serve trained models through a versioned REST API for sliding-window inference on new scans.

- Provide a web interface for uploading scans, viewing slice-by-slice segmentation overlays, and downloading a structured report.

- Track experiments, version datasets and models, and expose operational monitoring (latency, throughput, input drift).

- Be packaged and deployed via Docker containers with a documented CI/CD pipeline.

Out of scope: real-time intraoperative imaging, integration with a hospital PACS/EHR system beyond a DICOM-import stub, and any claim of regulatory (FDA/CE) clearance. The system is explicitly a research and portfolio-grade pipeline — see Section 14, Ethical, Legal, and Regulatory Considerations.

## **1.3 Intended Audience**

| **Audience** | **Interest in this Document** |
| --- | --- |
| ML / Software Engineer (you) | Primary implementer — uses this SRS as the build blueprint for every module. |
| Technical Reviewer / Mentor | Assesses architecture soundness, completeness, and engineering rigor. |
