## **1.4 Definitions, Acronyms and Abbreviations**

| **Term** | **Definition** |
| --- | --- |
| BraTS | Brain Tumor Segmentation benchmark dataset and challenge, multi-institutional multi-modal MRI with expert tumor annotations. |
| NIfTI | Neuroimaging Informatics Technology Initiative — .nii/.nii.gz volumetric medical image file format. |
| DICOM | Digital Imaging and Communications in Medicine — the clinical standard format for medical images. |
| MRI Modality (T1, T1ce, T2, FLAIR) | Four MRI sequences included per BraTS case; T1ce = post-contrast T1, FLAIR = fluid-attenuated inversion recovery. |
| ET / TC / WT | Enhancing Tumor / Tumor Core / Whole Tumor — the three overlapping tumor sub-region labels scored in BraTS. |
| Dice Coefficient | Overlap-based segmentation metric; 2×│A∩B│ / (│A│+│B│), range 0–1. |
| HD95 | 95th-percentile Hausdorff Distance — boundary-based segmentation error metric, in millimeters. |
| nnU-Net | Self-configuring U-Net framework that derives architecture and preprocessing from a dataset fingerprint. |
| Sliding-Window Inference | Technique for running a patch-trained model over a full volume by tiling overlapping patches. |
| ONNX | Open Neural Network Exchange — interoperable format for exporting trained models for inference. |
| API | Application Programming Interface. |
| CI/CD | Continuous Integration / Continuous Deployment. |
| PHI | Protected Health Information. |

